      "text": "## The Big Picture: The Circulation Is a Pressure/Flow/Volume System With a Self-Sealing Repair Layer"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEMODYNAMIC-DISORDERS-THROMBOSIS-AND-SHOCK.md#007",
      "path": [
        "03-HEMODYNAMIC-DISORDERS-THROMBOSIS-AND-SHOCK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:pathology:03-hemodynamic-disorders-thrombosis-and-shock]",
        "canonical_path": "pathology/03-HEMODYNAMIC-DISORDERS-THROMBOSIS-AND-SHOCK.md",
        "concepts": "[edema-congestion, hemostasis, virchow-triad, thrombosis-embolism-infarction, shock]",
        "current_path": "pathology/03-HEMODYNAMIC-DISORDERS-THROMBOSIS-AND-SHOCK.md",
        "id": "maxim:pathology:hemodynamic-disorders-thrombosis-and-shock",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "pathology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[hemodynamics]",
        "section": "pathology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Hemodynamic Disorders, Thrombosis, and Shock",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The novice mental model is \"blood flows in tubes; clots are bad; bleeding is bad.\" The expert\nmodel has two coupled control problems. The first is **fluid balance** — keeping the right\nvolume of fluid inside vessels against the forces trying to push it out, so that edema\n(too much fluid in tissue) and congestion (too much blood pooled in vessels) are *control\nfailures* of the same system. The second is **hemostasis** — a self-sealing repair layer that\nmust clot *exactly enough, exactly where a vessel is breached, and nowhere else*. Thrombosis,\nembolism, and infarction are what happen when the repair layer fires in the wrong place;\nshock is what happens when the whole pressure/flow/volume system loses the ability to perfuse\ntissue."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEMODYNAMIC-DISORDERS-THROMBOSIS-AND-SHOCK.md#008",
      "path": [
        "03-HEMODYNAMIC-DISORDERS-THROMBOSIS-AND-SHOCK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:pathology:03-hemodynamic-disorders-thrombosis-and-shock]",
        "canonical_path": "pathology/03-HEMODYNAMIC-DISORDERS-THROMBOSIS-AND-SHOCK.md",
        "concepts": "[edema-congestion, hemostasis, virchow-triad, thrombosis-embolism-infarction, shock]",
        "current_path": "pathology/03-HEMODYNAMIC-DISORDERS-THROMBOSIS-AND-SHOCK.md",
        "id": "maxim:pathology:hemodynamic-disorders-thrombosis-and-shock",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "pathology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[hemodynamics]",
        "section": "pathology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Hemodynamic Disorders, Thrombosis, and Shock",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHE HEMODYNAMIC SYSTEM  (this guide owns both control problems)\n==============================================================\n  CONTROL PROBLEM 1: FLUID BALANCE            CONTROL PROBLEM 2: HEMOSTASIS\n  ------------------------------              ----------------------------\n  keep fluid IN vessels                       clot ONLY at a breach, ONLY enough\n        |                                            |\n  failure: EDEMA (fluid -> tissue)            failure A: BLEEDING (clot too little)\n           CONGESTION (blood pools)           failure B: THROMBOSIS (clot wrong place)\n                                                     |\n                                              a thrombus can BREAK OFF -> EMBOLISM\n                                                     |\n                                              occlusion -> ISCHEMIA -> INFARCTION (see 01)"
    },
