        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Hemodynamic Disorders, Thrombosis, and Shock",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Two facts organize the guide. First, **the same machinery is protective and pathological**:\nhemostasis that seals a wound is the identical process that, misplaced, forms an occluding\nthrombus — pathology here is almost always *the right mechanism in the wrong context*. Second,\n**these disorders cascade**: a thrombus embolizes, an embolus occludes, an occlusion infarcts,\nand widespread perfusion failure is shock — so the guide is best read as a **connected chain**,\nnot a set of independent topics."
    }
